spec.text:
id: h6
card:
  lens: lead
  slug: prev-range-break
  contribution: method
  problem: "The gap family and h2 bet on the open or the whole session, so their P&L hinged on a few big gap days (concentration 1.00-3.14). Breaks of yesterday's high or low that happen inside the session, on days that opened inside yesterday's range, have not been tested at all."
  motivation: "Lesson from h1.2-h1.2.5: continuation existed but was carried by a few large-gap days and failed concentration and DSR. Removing gap days and requiring the break to happen during the session isolates a different event. A 1 ATR take cap stops any single trend day from carrying the net, which is the check every predecessor failed. The quiet-open clause reuses the gap family's own finding that gaps under ~0.3% behaved as noise."
  approach: "On days that open within 0.3% of yesterday's close, go long on the first 1-minute close above yesterday's high (short below yesterday's low) after 09:45, with a 0.5 ATR stop, a 1 ATR take and flat at 15:15."
  plan: "Features ph = prev_day(high), pl = prev_day(low), g = gap_pct, m = minute_of_day, atr(days 14). Entry long: close > ph and abs(g) < p.g and m >= 30; short: close < pl and abs(g) < p.g and m >= 30; max_per_day 1. Exit stop_atr 0.5, take_atr 1.0, time 15:15. CPCV over g in [0.002, 0.003, 0.005]; demo gate."
  mechanism: "Stop-loss and breakout buy-stop orders cluster just beyond the prior day's extremes (Osler 2005, stop-loss cascades in FX). When an in-session move reaches them, the triggered market orders push price further, and late breakout traders follow. The stop holders pay because their orders are placed for risk control, not price."
  rule: "long: close > prev_day high and abs(gap_pct) < p.g and minute_of_day >= 30; short mirror at prev_day low; stop 0.5 ATR, take 1 ATR, exit 15:15"
  kill:
    - "CPCV median path SR <= 0"
    - "best 5 days carry >= 50% of net despite the 1 ATR take cap"
    - "dropping the abs(gap_pct) clause does not hurt (ablation), i.e. it is just the gap family again"
    - "gross/costs < 3"
instrument: {segment: futures, underlying: NIFTY}
session: {start: "09:20", end: "15:15"}
features:
  # raw close is not an expression name; sma(close, 1) is the 1-minute close itself
  c: {fn: sma, field: close, n: 1}
  ph: {fn: prev_day, field: high}
  pl: {fn: prev_day, field: low}
  g: {fn: gap_pct}
  m: {fn: minute_of_day}
entry:
  long: "c > ph and abs(g) < p.g and m >= 30"
  short: "c < pl and abs(g) < p.g and m >= 30"
  max_per_day: 1
exit: {stop_atr: 0.5, take_atr: 1.0, atr_days: 14, time: "15:15"}
# card names no sizing; same as the reference example
sizing: {risk_per_trade: 0.01, capital_inr: 14040000, max_lots: 10}
params: {g: 0.003}
grid: {g: [0.002, 0.003, 0.005]}
